{"message":"I checked your Green and Blue accounts. Both accounts are open, and both cards are active with no fraud or temporary security blocks. However, your ATM withdrawals today have nearly used each card’s daily allowance: Green has approximately $250 remaining from its $600 daily limit, and Blue has approximately $100 remaining from its $500 daily limit. The ATM may also impose a lower limit of its own.

Because all three cards were declined at the same machine, please stop retrying there and try a different ATM—preferably a Rho-Bank ATM—with a smaller amount: no more than $250 on Green or $100 on Blue. If the ATM offers account types, choose checking.

Your daughter’s teen card may have a $150 daily ATM limit and parental controls, but I can’t inspect or change another account holder’s card from your verification. If you need more than the remaining amount, tell me which of your cards you want to use and the exact cash amount; I can check whether a 24-hour temporary limit increase is available. The Blue Account is not eligible based on a recent overdraft fee, while Green may still qualify."}
